<%= render "shared/public_page_meta",
      title: "State-Wise Professional Tax Guide for Payroll | Kula HR",
      description: "Understand Kula HR's supported Professional Tax states and verify current payroll rates and filing details on official state government portals.",
      canonical_path: professional_tax_guide_path %>

<%= render "home/landing/styles" %>
<%= render "resources/styles" %>
<%= render "home/landing/nav" %>

<main class="resource-page">
  <%= render "resources/hero",
        parent: "Resources",
        eyebrow: "Professional Tax guide",
        headline: "State rules need state sources.",
        lede: "Professional Tax is not one India-wide payroll table. Liability, salary slabs, special months, registration, payment and return rules vary by state or local body.",
        stamp: "Seven Kula HR configurations · Official links · No stale rate table" %>

  <section class="bg-white py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[.75fr_1.25fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[.16em] text-kula-700">Before calculation</p>
          <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-950">Resolve the place, period and current schedule.</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <% [
            ["01", "Applicable location", "Confirm the employee work location and the employer registration relevant to that payroll."],
            ["02", "Current schedule", "Open the official state or local-body source; do not carry last year’s slab forward by assumption."],
            ["03", "Payment & return", "Record the applicable frequency, due date, challan and return evidence for the employer."]
          ].each do |number, title, body| %>
            <li class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-6">
              <span class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-marigold-700"><%= number %></span>
              <h3 class="mt-6 text-base font-bold text-stone-950"><%= title %></h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-6 text-stone-600"><%= body %></p>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <% @states.each_with_index do |(state, authority, url), index| %>
          <article class="resource-paper flex min-h-56 flex-col rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-7">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-5">
              <span class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-kula-700"><%= format("%02d", index + 1) %></span>
              <span class="rounded-full bg-kula-50 px-3 py-1 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-kula-800">Configured</span>
            </div>
            <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-950"><%= state %></h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-6 text-stone-500"><%= authority %></p>
            <a href="<%= url %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mt-auto pt-7 text-sm font-semibold text-kula-800 underline decoration-kula-300 underline-offset-4">Open official source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </article>
        <% end %>
        <article class="flex min-h-56 flex-col rounded-2xl border-2 border-dashed border-stone-300 bg-stone-50 p-7">
          <span class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-stone-500">OTHER</span>
          <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900">Another state or local body?</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-6 text-stone-600">Do not force a nearby state’s configuration. Confirm applicability and contact Kula HR before processing payroll.</p>
          <a href="<%= contact_path %>" class="mt-auto pt-7 text-sm font-semibold text-kula-800">Ask about support →</a>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12">
        <%= render "resources/review_note", reviewed: @last_reviewed, text: "The configured-state list describes current Kula HR product coverage, not a legal statement that every employer in those states owes tax. Official schedules and local rules control." %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 py-16 sm:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-10 px-6 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:px-8">
      <article class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-8">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[.16em] text-kula-700">In Kula HR</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-bold text-stone-950">Keep PT visible in payroll review.</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-stone-600">Supported state slabs are stored per company and the calculated deduction remains a separate payslip line. That makes it possible to compare the applied value with the state source before approving the payroll run.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-8">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[.16em] text-kula-700">In your evidence</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-bold text-stone-950">Retain more than the deduction.</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-stone-600">Keep the schedule or notification used, payroll register, state payment challan, return acknowledgement and any documented exception together for the relevant period.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<%= render "home/landing/footer" %>
<%= render "marketing_pages/scripts" %>
